2. THE ITEM BANKS AND THE WRITING — all rights reserved
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Everything under src/instruments/*/i18n/ and src/ui/i18n/ — the questionnaire
items, the result prose, and the four translations of both — is copyright
© 2026 Aleksander Dudek. All rights reserved. It is not covered by the MIT
grant above and may not be copied, reproduced or redistributed without
permission.

This split is not an afterthought. Questionnaire items are exactly the kind of
work that gets lifted from one product into another, and the reason every
folder in this repository writes its own items is that the published
instruments they are modelled on are themselves protected. Taking that position
seriously means taking it in both directions.

Each instrument folder carries a provenance.js recording what its construct is,
where the construct came from, whether it is public, and which named
instruments were deliberately not used. Those files are the record of what was
borrowed — the idea — and what was not — the questions.

None of the item banks here has been validated, normed or administered to a
sample. They are original writing against public constructs, and they carry no
inherited psychometric properties from the instruments that established those
constructs.
